<title>FRANCE: Algerian, Malaysian firms sign $38 mln oil deal.</title>
<headline>Algerian, Malaysian firms sign $38 mln oil deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria's state-owned oil and gas firm Sonatrach and the Malaysian company Petronas Carigali signed a $38 million oil exploration contract on Wednesday, the Algerian official news agency APS said.</p>
<p>Under the deal, Petronas Carigali, a subsidiary of the Malaysian state company Petronas, will carry out seismic research and sink four exploration wells, the agency said.</p>
<p>The contract is a &quot;production-sharing&quot; deal, under which both companies will benefit from any commercial finds. The Malaysian firm will operate in an area northwest of Algeria's main oilfield, Hassi Messaoud, in the Sahara Desert.</p>
</text>
